  "why_this_exists": "A clone replays one bundle per head, and each replay leaves its own packfile. Git resolves objects by consulting pack indexes in turn, so at thousands of packs both delta resolution and ordinary lookup begin to scale with pack count, and per-head clone cost stops being flat. This arm is the measurement that showed it: ms/head rises with depth instead of holding constant. The fix is a periodic multi-pack-index refresh during replay (safehub-cli common::maybe_refresh_multi_pack_index); the headline depth cells in depth-clone-latest.json are measured on the fixed build.",
